</div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Created By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n        <div class=\"topic-examples\">\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/mark-rein-hagen\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Created By\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Mark Rein·Hagen</strong>\n                    <span>Mark Rein•Hagen (often written Rein-Hagen) is a roleplaying, card, computer and board game designer.</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/mark-rein-hagen\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Mark Rein·Hagen\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Rein·Hagen created Vampire: The Masquerade.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Part Of</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Part Of\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/world-of-darkness\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            World of Darkness\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Vampire is a core World of Darkness game.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Publishes</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Publishes\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/white-wolf\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            White Wolf\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>White Wolf originally published Vampire.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Vampire: The Masquerade is also referenced as VtM, Vampire Masquerade, Vampire the Masquerade.</li><li>Rein·Hagen created Vampire: The Masquerade.</li><li>Players portray Kindred in Vampire.</li><li>Vampire is a core World of Darkness game.</li><li>White Wolf originally published Vampire.</li><li>Evidence around Vampire: The Masquerade is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Vampire: The Masquerade?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        Vampire: The Masquerade is a tabletop role-playing game (tabletop RPG) created by Mark Rein-Hagen and released in 1991 by <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/white-wolf\" class=\"entity-link\">White Wolf</a> Publishing as the first of several Storyteller System games for its <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/world-of-darkness\" class=\"entity-link\">World of Darkness</a> setting line.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Vampire: The Masquerade is the first <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/world-of-darkness\" class=\"entity-link\">World of Darkness</a> game and the first Storyteller System game published by <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/white-wolf\" class=\"entity-link\">White Wolf</a>. A major departure from the more power and heroics oriented games of the era, VTM is a game of personal horror. It is the parent and the most popular of all the <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/world-of-darkness\" class=\"entity-link\">World of Darkness</a> games, and was the genesis of almost all the major ideas people associate with <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/white-wolf\" class=\"entity-link\">White Wolf</a>.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        In Vampire: The Masquerade, the players assume the role of vampires, immortal beings cursed with an unquenchable thirst for blood and vulnerability to sunlight – creatures forever bound to their inner Beast (the animal urges of hunger, fear and rage). It is a game of personal horror, as the characters are continually forced to walk a moral tightrope between their need to survive and the horrific means by which they ensure it.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Vampires are one of the three main supernatural races in the <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/world-of-darkness\" class=\"entity-link\">World of Darkness</a> and the fundamental characters of Vampire: The Masquerade and its spinoff games like Vampire: The Dark Ages and <a href=\"/vampire-the-masquerade/kindred\" class=\"entity-link\">Kindred</a> of the East. The article above offers a closer look at vampires, with their physiology, their politics and their clan division.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        VtM, Vampire Masquerade, Vampire the Masquerade.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":958,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"d3033f0e-454c-4ed2-a29f-ba0773712c28","name":"Vampire: The Masquerade","slug":"vampire-the-masquerade","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"Vampire: The Masquerade is a tabletop role-playing game (tabletop RPG) created by Mark Rein-Hagen and released in 1991 by White Wolf Publishing as the first of several Storyteller System games for its World of Darkness…","description":"Vampire: The Masquerade is a tabletop role-playing game (tabletop RPG) created by Mark Rein-Hagen and released in 1991 by White Wolf Publishing as the first of several Storyteller System games for its World of Darkness setting line.\n\nVampire: The Masquerade is the first World of Darkness game and the first Storyteller System game published by White Wolf. A major departure from the more power and heroics oriented games of the era, VTM is a game of personal horror. It is the parent and the most popular of all the World of Darkness games, and was the genesis of almost all the major ideas people associate with White Wolf.\n\nIn Vampire: The Masquerade, the players assume the role of vampires, immortal beings cursed with an unquenchable thirst for blood and vulnerability to sunlight – creatures forever bound to their inner Beast (the animal urges of hunger, fear and rage). It is a game of personal horror, as the characters are continually forced to walk a moral tightrope between their need to survive and the horrific means by which they ensure it.\n\nVampires are one of the three main supernatural races in the World of Darkness and the fundamental characters of Vampire: The Masquerade and its spinoff games like Vampire: The Dark Ages and Kindred of the East. The article above offers a closer look at vampires, with their physiology, their politics and their clan division.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"vampire-the-masquerade","aliases":["VtM","Vampire Masquerade","Vampire the Masquerade"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"con